<ResourceDictionary xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">
    <!-- ═══ SOLAR FLARE THEME ═══

         A preset is its GEOMETRY plus a seed. The colours come from Shared/FallbackPalette.axaml
         until ThemeService.ApplyCustomization lands, and from the M3 generator after that; this
         preset's seed (#FFB800) lives in Models/SeedPreset.cs. (RemEx-2gjwn)

         THIS IS THE LIGHT PRESET, and that is now a SETTING rather than a property of the name.
         The catalog pins IsLight = true for it explicitly. The fallback palette merged
         below is dark, so this preset is the one that would show a dark flash if the generated
         palette ever arrived after the first frame - the price of one fallback instead of four.

         IT DOES NOT FLASH, BUT NOT BECAUSE ANYTHING IS SYNCHRONOUS. ApplyCustomization posts its
         whole body to the dispatcher (ThemeService.ApplyCustomization), and MainWindow.Show happens
         from InitializeAppAsync, queued after it. What actually orders them is priority: the post is
         DispatcherPriority.Default, which runs ahead of Render, so it lands before the first frame.
         Lower that priority, or move Show ahead of it, and this preset flashes dark.
    -->
    <ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
        <ResourceInclude Source="avares://Remex.Desktop/Themes/Shared/FallbackPalette.axaml"/>
    </ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>

    <!-- Soft, generous corners and a barely-there shadow: the daylight look. -->
    <CornerRadius x:Key="CardCornerRadius">24</CornerRadius>
    <Thickness x:Key="CardBorderThickness">1</Thickness>
    <!-- ELEVATION RAMP (RemEx-qbzl1). One shadow vocabulary for every raised surface, so a
         Card, a dialog and an app bar say "level 2" rather than each inventing a BoxShadows.
         Levels track Material's depth ramp in ORDER, not in absolute values: Material's
         ShadowProvider is a fixed black drop shadow, while RemEx's is soft, accent-tinted and
         scaled live by the GlowStrength slider. ThemeService overrides all four on every
         ApplyCustomization; these literals are what a theme file alone renders with.
           1 = resting surface (cards, list panels)
           2 = raised resting (selected/pinned cards, the app bar)
           3 = hover / interactive lift
         A fourth level lands when Phase 5 raises dialogs and the tray flyout; adding it now
         would be a key with no consumer.
         Replaces CardShadow/CardHoverShadow, which named the same two steps after the ONE
         control that used them and had no room for a third. -->
    <BoxShadows x:Key="Elevation1Shadow">0 4 16 0 #1A000000</BoxShadows>
    <BoxShadows x:Key="Elevation2Shadow">0 6 24 0 #24000000</BoxShadows>
    <BoxShadows x:Key="Elevation3Shadow">0 8 32 0 #30000000, 0 0 12 2 #40FFB800</BoxShadows>
</ResourceDictionary>
